,000 a month. You spend"}, {"start": 10.86, "end": 17.0, "text": " 1900 and you save 100. Your salary goes up to $3,000. A year later, you spend"}, {"start": 17.0, "end": 22.84, "text": " 2,900 and you're still saving 100. This is called lifestyle inflation."}, {"start": 23.44, "end": 28.08, "text": " Often, every raise becomes the new normal and spending rises to meet it."}, {"start": 28.880000000000003, "end": 32.62, "text": " Behind it is a psychological mechanism, hedonic adaptation."}, {"start": 33.36, "end": 37.84, "text": " Our brain gets used to improvements fast. The bigger apartment, the Friday dinner"}, {"start": 37.84, "end": 42.24, "text": " out, the more comfortable car. After a few months, it's no longer a luxury."}, {"start": 42.64, "end": 46.1, "text": " It's the minimum. Psychologists call it the hedonic treadmill."}, {"start": 46.58, "end": 48.84, "text": " You keep running, but you stay in the same place."}, {"start": 49.6, "end": 53.86, "text": " And the trap is that each upgrade looks reasonable. A slightly pricier"}, {"start": 53.86, "end": 59.0, "text": " rent, one more subscription, one more trip. No single expense is crazy, but"}, {"start": 59.0, "end": 63.8, "text": " together they swallow the entire raise. So how do you get out of it?"}, {"start": 64.28, "end": 68.52, "text": " First, look at your savings rate, not your salary. What matters isn't what"}, {"start": 68.52, "end": 73.24, "text": " you earn, it's what you keep. Then apply a simple rule to every raise."}, {"start": 73.74, "end": 77.16, "text": " Half goes to savings or investing before your lifestyle adjusts."}, {"start": 77.38, "end": 81.64, "text": " You can enjoy the other half without guilt. Finally, choose your upgrades."}, {"start": 81.64, "end": 86.38, "text": " One or two that truly make you happier. Not everyone your new salary allows."}, {"start": 87.02000000000001, "end": 90.14, "text": " Earning more doesn't make you rich. Keeping more does."}, {"start": 90.84, "end": 93.48, "text": " And you, which expense has appeared since your last raise?"}, {"start": 93.92, "end": 94.62, "text": " Tell us in the comments."}], "aligned_to_script": true}